        rdfs:label "docs/media/sponge_spicule_hexactin_bending_fracture.gif (generated output)" ;
        dcterms:description "10-frame bending-fracture GIF regenerated by the default invocation — docs/media/sponge_spicule_hexactin_bending_fracture.gif: rendered output of models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py at a69596cc, image/gif, 487114 B, 1092×482 px, 10 frames, artifact_sha256 53b04806cd2101c05b798952a15202673519520f8737bd04f8399860751a820a (sha256 53b04806cd2101c05b798952a15202673519520f8737bd04f8399860751a820a), spec_fingerprint e8c71f657d97f3086b3a9576cab7f81ff7eec29a8903ce345cec0985c35812ca" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Pass 3 remediated assessment; Phase B scoring pass executed by a Claude Fable 5.1 subagent from the Phase A handoff and diff)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics, cohesive-zone laminate bending, helical cage ridges and basalia waveguiding — Reproducibility package: 91/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Deterministic (no RNG; bitwise two-run check L2091-2094), `--self-test` passes all 12 checks in ~5 s (8 Pass 2 + 4 Pass 3 at L2096-2143: FE parity, cohesive-law integral, graceful vs catastrophic with identical first-crack load, fused = monolith, k_cat -> N monotone, psi_opt = 45 deg, parallel-axis identity, ray trace vs TIR, Gloge bracket, single mode at 2 um, PASS3_JSON present, 18 measurements), default render ~5.5 s producing the main PNG, growth GIF, Pass 3 mechanics PNG and bending-fracture GIF, and `--skip-pass3` / `--skip-gif` shorten the run. Deductions: `--seed` is accepted but does nothing (L2160) (-2); the two PNGs are excluded by the repository `.gitignore` (*.png) so the rendered figures are not tracked artefacts (pre-existing convention) (-2); no requirements lock or recorded SHA-256 of the rendered outputs in the script itself (-3); the self-test asserts the specimen angle against the JSON copy of its own output (L2087) (-2)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L2160–L2160: --seed is a documented no-op <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L2160-L2160>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-repro-package-3> ;
